  "answer_verification": {
    "status": "needs_review",
    "verified_answer": "68.34 degrees (using rounded AW=8.49 cm); exact dimensions give 68.35 degrees",
    "issue": "The word ?Now? signals dependence on the rounded result from the preceding part. Using AW rounded to 8.49 cm gives 68.34 degrees; using exact AW=12/sqrt(2) gives 68.35 degrees. Preserve raw GT 68.34.",
    "reasoning": "cos(theta)=AW/VA. With prior-part rounding: arccos(8.49/23)=68.34 degrees. Without intermediate rounding, arccos((12/sqrt(2))/23)=68.35 degrees. This is a rounding-dependence issue."
  },
